# Agent containment (Cybersec Phase-1)

Keep offensive/agent workers off the host trust boundary. Human installs Lume/CUA VM when needed.

## Architecture

- Prefer **VM/OS sandbox** (CUA / Lume) for Tier-2 browser or OS-control agents; do not run untrusted agent workers on the host desktop session.
- Secrets and orchestrator API keys stay on the **orchestrator**; workers get least privilege and no `docker.sock`.
- Ban `--network=host` (and equivalent) for agent workers — AIRecon / agent-phishing kill-chain finding.

## Lab sandboxes

- Defending-code / gVisor / Docker reference harnesses: **laptop lab only** — not cemini-prod deploy.
- AOHP (AOSP agent-native OS): lab-validate security-policy hooks before any production agent use; treat as large REFERENCE tree unless explicitly scoped.
- Autoresearch / red-team victim containers: owned Docker sandboxes with written authorization only.

## Human gates

- Lume/CUA VM install and Codex sidecar consent are operator-only — agents document, do not pretend installed.
- No curl|sh bootstrap for containment stacks.
